// The framework's own program.
//
// No `paths` at all: the seams are declared in `package.json`'s `imports`, where `#shared` / `#ui` /
// `#server` / `#compiler` mean THIS package's directories and the same four names mean an APP's
// directories inside an app. That is the whole reason they are subpath imports rather than tsconfig
// aliases — `paths` is PROGRAM-global, so an app whose program compiles this package's source (a
// workspace link resolves to `.ts`) would have to declare the framework's aliases to type-check its
// own pages. `imports` is package-scoped, and Bun, `tsc` and `Bun.build` all resolve it the same way.
//
// The public specifiers — `abide`, `abide/ui`, `abide/server`, `abide/compiler` — are what an APP
// resolves through, and are deliberately not reachable from inside here by any shorter name.
{
    "extends": "../../tsconfig.json",
    "include": ["abide.ts", "src/**/*.ts", "compiler/**/*.ts", "cli/**/*.ts"]
}
